# centralize_events_lobby_name_change_udp — client 2 (slot 1).
# Joins after a short delay so client 1 lands in slot 0 first.
# Ops fire against the per-iteration pump-tick fallback while
# serverTick is still 0 (lobby phase). c2 renames in lobby
# (after c1's rename, before either client has readied), then
# readies BEFORE c1 — see c1's stream for the readiness order.
#
# The rename mirrors c1's: today the server filters out the
# renamer when broadcasting PACKET_NAME_CHANGE, so c2's golden
# will NOT contain a CTRL_PLAYER_NAME entry for its own rename
# — but it WILL contain one for c1's rename above.
{"tick": 100,  "op": "set_team",    "slot": 1, "team": 2}
{"tick": 700,  "op": "name_change", "slot": 1, "name": "Renamed2"}
{"tick": 2000, "op": "set_ready",   "slot": 1, "ready": true}
